BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watershed Literary Event: A Reading with N. West Moss &amp\; Matth
 ew Thorburn
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261101T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261101T180000
UID:7c11815aa92878ba681ee2a0ff788ec4@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:NOTE NEW DATE: NOV 1! Join us Sunday\, November 1st\, at 3 PM 
 at the South Orange Skate House in Meadowland Park for an afternoon of rea
 dings featuring memoir and fiction writer N. West Moss and poet Matthew Th
 orburn. N. West Moss is the author of Flesh &amp\; Blood\, The Subway Stop
 s at Bryant Park\, and the middle grade novel Birdy. Her work has appeared
  in The New York Times\, McSweeney’s\, and The Saturday Evening Post\, a
 mong other publications. Matthew Thorburn is the author of six books of po
 etry\, including The Grace of Distance and Dear Almost. His new collection
 \, A Hundred Birds\, is forthcoming from LSU Press in Spring 2027. Founded
  in 2019\, Watershed Literary Events celebrates talented and diverse write
 rs with a New Jersey connection. Free and open to the public! Watershed is
  sponsored by the South Orange Department of Recreation and Cultural Affai
 rs and the Meadowland Park Conservancy. South Orange Skate House\, Meadowl
 and Park Sunday\, November 1st 3 PM Come hear some wonderful local literar
 y voices and celebrate the return of Watershed! N. West Moss: Kristine Bil
 kau | Matthew Thorburn: K.Loo THEME: OPEN MIC / FEATURE HOST: South Orange
  Village / Theresa Burns FEATURES: Matthew Thorburn PRICE: FREE CONTACT: F
 B - South Orange Village / Theresa Burns
LOCATION:South Orange Skate House\, Meadowland Park\, 5 Mead Street\, Sout
 h Orange Village\, NJ\, 07079
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/watershed-literary-event-a-rea
 ding-with-n-west-moss-matthew-thorburn
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
