BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JERSEY CITY WRITERS: ONE-MIC STAND
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261113T220000
UID:9c971bcfb26d4cb1742c278114855854@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:@sjbythegram THIS IS IT!! We saved the best for last. This wil
 l be the last One Mic Stand with SJ of 2026 and we are ending this year wi
 th a killer show. Our features Natalie Ilda and Mario Rubio from HOT PEOPL
 E READ POETRY will grace the stage and bring the . Plus Special Guest Deli
 lah Saul\, a documentarian and founder of @outlawmediacpmpany will also be
  in attendance as we will have our collaboration with Hot People Read Poet
 ry on Nov 20th when they will have their event in Jersey City!! You don’
 t want to miss a thing!! Natalie Gilda believes SWers are inherent storyte
 llers\, which is what makes them such amazing writers. She is the creator 
 and host of Hot People Read Poetry\, a SWer founded and focused open mic e
 xperience and poetry show in NYC. She also cohosts an interview series\, P
 ink Dancing Poets. Maria Rubio (she/they) is a born and raised New Yorker 
 with roots in the Philippines. Her writing explores everything that she co
 mes in contact with as a Brown queer woman who is building community withi
 n the belly of capitalism. Delilah Saul is a SWer\, documentarian\, and fo
 under of @outlawmediacompany. Her recent film\, “Beloved”\, explores t
 he impact of stigma on the love lives of SWers. She’s currently directin
 g and producing a documentary about media bias against SWers. She hosts SW
  + LOVE\, a podcast about navigating personal relationships as a SWer. THE
 ME: OPEN MIC / FEATURES HOST: SJ FEATURES: Delilah Saul / Natalie Gilda / 
 Maria Rubio PRICE: $10 suggested donation (Cash\, Venmo\, Paypal) CONTACT:
  @sjbythegram
LOCATION:157B 1st Street\, 6th Floor\, Jersey City\, NJ
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/jersey-city-writers-one-mic-st
 and
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
